    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "01. Core Concepts",
    "ruleNumber": "01.02",
    "summary": "A unit acts together. Its opening model count sets Starting Strength, including attached models. Compare remaining wounds to W for a unit that started with one model. Otherwise compare the number of survivors with the opening count. Exactly half qualifies as Half-Strength. Splitting before battle resets each resulting unit’s count. A qualifying model can satisfy a unit descriptor. An effect that gives the unit a rule applies across its models.",
